-- title:
--   Branch ideals are prime in the localised λ-node ring
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be an odd prime, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$, let $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$ be a ring homomorphism, and let $l\in k$ satisfy $l^{q^2}=l$. Let $K$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb Q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, put $A_0=\mathrm{coeffSubring}\,A\,K=A\cap K$, and let $\mathrm{redRestrict}\,\mathrm{red}\,K\colon A_0\to k$ be the restriction of $\mathrm{red}$ along $A_0\subseteq A$. Let $\varpi\in A_0$ be such that an element $c\in A_0$ reduces to $0$ precisely when $c=\varpi d$ for some $d\in A_0$. Write $\Lambda$ for the homomorphism `lambdaEval` from $A_0[X_0,X_1]$ to Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ sending a coefficient to the corresponding constant series, $X_0$ to the $\lambda$-series `lambdaModC` and $X_1$ to its level-$q$ expansion `lambdaNModC`, and let $R_0$ be the subring `lambdaLocalizedAtPoint` of Laurent series consisting of all $f$ with $f\,\Lambda(s)=\Lambda(r)$ for some $r,s\in A_0[X_0,X_1]$ whose $s$ has nonzero value at $(l,l^q)$ after reduction of coefficients by $\mathrm{redRestrict}\,\mathrm{red}\,K$. Then, inside $R_0$: the ideal generated by $\Lambda(\varpi)$ and $\Lambda(X_1-X_0^q)$ is prime, it does not contain $\Lambda(X_0-X_1^q)$, and it contains no $\Lambda(X_0-c)$ with $c\in A_0$; and (stated as an implication whose hypothesis $l^{q^2}=l$ is already assumed) the ideal generated by $\Lambda(\varpi)$ and $\Lambda(X_0-X_1^q)$ is prime and does not contain $\Lambda(X_1-X_0^q)$.
--
--   This is the assertion that the two branches through the point $(l,l^q)$ of the special fibre of the level-$q$ plane model in the Legendre $\lambda$-coordinate cut out prime ideals of the local ring at that point, together with the non-membership statements distinguishing the two branches and separating them from the horizontal divisors $\lambda=c$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.LambdaNodeLocalized.isNoetherianRing_isLocalRing_lambdaLocalizedAtPoint_coeffSubring`](thm.html#ModularCurve.LambdaNodeLocalized.isNoetherianRing_isLocalRing_lambdaLocalizedAtPoint_coeffSubring) and by [`ModularCurve.isIntegrallyClosed_lambdaLocalizedAtPoint_coeffSubring`](thm.html#ModularCurve.isIntegrallyClosed_lambdaLocalizedAtPoint_coeffSubring) in the study of this local ring; the proof quotes `pointEval_eq_zero_of_lambdaEval_eq_zero_of_ne_two` and `eval2_branch_eq_zero_of_lambdaEval_eq_zero`.
